# The machines tell their state by light and body, proven through the real keys
# on a normal seed-1 coast late at night: a harvester working a dark field with
# its lamps and their wash on the row ahead, its windup brightening the comb; a
# watcher's stipple beam sweeping; a real hit stuttering its lights out; and a
# kill, where the lights go in order and the working part goes last; then a
# runner coming after you with its lights held locked.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/machines.tour --seed=1 --hour=22.5 --weather=clear:0
# A runner coming after you: its walk is a hunt, so the slit's scan holds dead
# centre and its eyes stay hot all the way in, never looking round as on an errand.
at 132,366
zoom 7
coast calm
wait 1.0
spawn runner
wait 0.8
walk 0,1 0.5 run
shot 00-runner-hunts-lights-locked
walk 0,1 0.4 run
shot 00b-still-locked-as-it-comes
coast calm
zoom 9
# A harvester's field on the first coast.
coast calm
at 200.5,431.5
wait 1.5
spawn harvester
wait 1.2
shot 01-harvester-working-at-night
await tell 6
wait 0.3
shot 02-windup-brightens-the-working-side
tap dodge
wait 0.1
tap dodge
wait 0.6
# Away from it, to a watcher out in a field, drawn back so its mast shows.
at 130,370
zoom 13
wait 1.5
coast calm
spawn watcher
wait 2.5
shot 03-watcher-beam-sweeps
walkto mob 2
wait 0.3
shot 04-watcher-locks-on
try 6
walkto part 1
tap swing
await hit 1.5
end
wait 0.1
shot 05-hurt-lights-stutter
try 30
walkto part 1
tap swing
await killed 1.2
end
wait 0.12
shot 06-dying-lights-go-in-order
wait 0.6
shot 07-dead-and-dark
